// Metadata for the "soldier_meshy" character — see docs/CHARACTER_IMPORT_CHECKLIST.md's
// "Scale and origin" section for why this can't just trust the mesh's native
// scale/pivot.
//
// This mesh shipped lying on its back, facing the camera instead of away
// from it (a Meshy-export quirk zombie_meshy.glb also had) — both fixed
// PERMANENTLY in the asset itself with scripts/normalize_glb_root_rotation.py
// (X +90° to stand it up, then Y +180° to face the right way, composed
// together into the scene root node's own rotation — see that script's own
// doc comment). facing_deg stays 0.0 below because of that, same as it
// would for any other fully-normalized mesh; if a fresh re-export of this
// asset ever needs re-normalizing, redo both axes in one run rather than
// reaching for a runtime facing_deg workaround.
//
// scale/y_offset are F9-tunable (EDITOR=1): third-person (KeyU),
// Comma/Period nudges scale, Minus/Equal nudges y_offset — see
// nudge_player_model_tuning/save_player_model_tuning
// (crates/client/src/movement_combat.rs). `animations` isn't nudge-able,
// only hand-edited.
//
// mesh/anim_source are two SEPARATE glb files (scripts/extract_glb_mesh_only.py
// and scripts/extract_glb_animations.py, run against the original combined
// export) — mesh has zero animations of its own; every clip below is
// loaded from anim_source instead.
//
// POLICY: anim_source lives under THIS character's own characters/
// soldier_meshy/anims/ folder now, NOT a cross-character shared one —
// mesh/anim still split into 2 files (keeps tooling uniform), but no
// longer shared with any other rig's mesh. Used to live at
// characters/_shared_anims/mixamo_base.glb and also be pointed at by
// crates/shared's ZOMBIE_SOLDIER_ANIM_PATH (zombie_soldier, a different
// character's rig) — retired after a confirmed incident: bone-name/
// hierarchy matching between the 2 rigs wasn't enough, because
// bevy_animation clips set each joint's LOCAL rotation to an ABSOLUTE
// value every keyframe (not a delta from rest), so playback is only
// correct if the target joint's own rest rotation means the same thing
// this clip's source rig's did — zombie_soldier's didn't (confirmed:
// wrong Hips->Foot world-space direction), and 2 separate attempts to fix
// it by rewriting zombie_soldier's rest pose to match (scripts/
// retarget_rest_pose.py) both failed, the second one catastrophically
// (deformed mesh, not just wrong pose). soldier_meshy itself was always
// fine here — this file's clips were authored FOR this exact rig
// originally, the mismatch was only ever an issue for the OTHER
// character borrowing it.
(
    id: "soldier_meshy",
    display_name: "Soldier (Meshy)",
    lore_ref: "docs/characters/soldier.md",

    mesh: "characters/soldier_meshy/mesh/soldier_meshy.glb",
    // See docs/CHARACTER_IMPORT_CHECKLIST.md before replacing this mesh.
    anim_source: "characters/soldier_meshy/anims/mixamo_base.glb",
    scale: 1.04,
    y_offset: -0.76,
    facing_deg: 0.0,

    // Indices into anim_source (mixamo_base.glb), not mesh.
    animations: (
        idle: 15,
        walk: 15,
        run: 4,
        run_back: 11,
        shoot: 3,
        death: 0,
    ),

    audio: [],
)
